Self-signed test certificate that expired on 2020-04-01, for SEC-07.
An expiry in the past is permanently inside any warning threshold, which is what makes the
degraded-status test deterministic: a short-dated certificate generated at test time would pass
today and start failing on whatever date it lapsed. rustls loads this happily -- a server does not
validate its own certificate's dates -- so it exercises the reporting path and nothing else.
